    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.backeted\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nRelevant treesitter config:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('nvim-treesitter.configs').setup {\r\n  -- ensure_installed = 'maintained',\r\n  ensure_installed = { 'bash', 'c', 'cpp', 'julia', 'lua', 'python', 'rust', 'typescript', 'vim', 'vimdoc', 'zig' },\r\n  auto_install = true,\r\n\r\n  highlight = {\r\n    enable = false,\r\n    additional_vim_regex_highlighting = false,\r\n    -- nvim gcc/c-family/c-common.cc from git://gcc.gnu.org/git/gcc.git\r\n    -- freezes editor and configured clangd provides us with highlighting\r\n    -- zig does not need treesitter for highlighting (zls also provides info)\r\n    disable = { 'c', 'cpp', 'zig' },\r\n  },\r\n  -- Note, that vib also works for blocks (symbols might be desirable)\r\n  incremental_selection = {\r\n    enable = false,\r\n    keymaps = {\r\n      init_selection = '<leader>vs',\r\n      node_decremental = 'gsN',\r\n      node_incremental = 'gsn',\r\n      scope_incremental = 'gss',\r\n    },\r\n    disable = { 'c', 'cpp', 'zig' }, -- slow, so opt-in\r\n  },\r\n  indent = {\r\n    enable = false,\r\n    disable = { 'c', 'cpp', 'python', 'zig' }, -- broken\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nHEAD master\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal1.lua some.cpp` (without mini.bracketed) [T and ]T have no effect. Also only installing mini.bracketed has no effect as the config is not run:\r\n```lua\r\n  {\r\n    'echasnovski/mini.bracketed',\r\n    version = false,\r\n    config = function() require('mini.bracketed').setup {} end,\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n2. `nvim -nu minimal2.lua some.cpp` (with mini.bracketed installed) [T and ]T jump to treesitter objects, even though I dont want to use treesitter.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNo active treesitter. Upstream should provide a sane way to decide, if treesitter is active or not and/or at least a convention how plugins should provide an interface instead of only offering it per plugin https://neovim.discourse.group/t/check-if-treesitter-is-enabled-in-the-current-buffer/902 and guessing if the config has been run or changed with `:TSConfigInfo`.\r\n\r\nTreesitter should be configurable as opt-in due to problematic behavior ie \r\n`nvim gcc/c-family/c-common.cc` from git://gcc.gnu.org/git/gcc.git freezes editor and configured clangd provides  highlighting. (runs out of memory, but thats another story)\r\n\r\nUpcoming changes https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/issues/4767 might provide this.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nActive treesitter.",
