            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am not sure I follow you here.\r\n\r\nHere is what I see:\r\n- You have tree-sitter for 'cpp' installed (it is listed in `ensure_installed`), which means that is is automatically attached to a buffer with `cpp` filetype. You can verify this by running `:InspectTree` in `cpp` buffer without 'mini.bracketed' installed: it should show parsed tree structure (although you disabled all its built-in capabilities).\r\n- Yes, mappings `[T` and `]T` don't work without 'mini.bracketed' and do work with 'mini.bracketed' (as they are defined in it).\r\n\r\nIf you don't want tree-sitter for `c` and `cpp`, is there something preventing you from *not installing* specific parsers?",
