        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Ugh. I really dont like the behavior of `installed == loading`.\r\n\r\nIf you don't want to use it at all, then not installing at all seems reasonable. If you want to use for something else (like textobjects with 'mini.ai' or `treesitter` target in 'mini.bracketed'), but not for highlighting/indent, then your current setup seems doing just like that. It is usually an automated usage of queries (like highlight, indent, etc.) that results into overall slowdown.\r\n\r\nClosing, as there seems to be no problem with 'mini.nvim'.",
